--

Was KNOWNBUG since round 152 ("conversion from 'signed int [5l]' to 'struct
_Partial'").  Fixed 2026-09-24 by seven front-end fixes along the libstdc++
range-adaptor chain: [dcl.init.aggr]/1 a constructor template disqualifies
the aggregate (ref_view{arr}); [temp.spec.partial.order] variable-template
partial specializations are ordered (extent_v<int[5]>); [temp.deduct.call]/3
no forwarding reference in a constructor-derived deduction guide and
[dcl.init.general]/9 value-initialising a reference is an error
(owning_view{declval<int(&)[5]>()}); [temp.constr.decl]/1 a requires-clause
is looked up from the template's scope (the hidden friend operator|);
[temp.variadic]/5 `Args...` in a requires-clause concept-id expands to the
deduced arity (__adaptor_partial_app_viable); [stmt.if]/2 no return type
deduction from a discarded `if constexpr` branch (_All::operator());
[temp.inst]/4 a body whose eager conversion fails while a class is being
elaborated is re-queued instead of dropped (view_interface members and the
ranges::begin(ref_view&) instance).  Exercised by the cpp20_ranges_* unit
tests.
Tagged broken-libstdcxx16 (temporary): with the libstdc++ 16 headers
`arr | views::take(3)' is rejected; root cause
cpp20_concept_disjunction_first_operand_substitution_failure (KNOWNBUG).
Remove the tag when that is fixed.
